      "caseHtml": "<section class=\"mc-case-current\" aria-label=\"Casustekst bij deze vraag\"><p class=\"mc-case-current-label\">Nodig voor deze vraag</p><h3>Opgave 2 (65 punten)</h3><h4>DEEL 1: 45 punten</h4><p>Een onderzoeker wil aan de hand van een steekproef van 100 willekeurige occasions kijken of de korting die een koper krijgt op de aanschaf van een occasion afhankelijk is van de leeftijd, het bruto jaarinkomen (euro) en geslacht (man = 0, vrouw = 1). Men onderzoekt de aannames dat de korting groter is bij:</p><p class=\"sra-case-list-item\">jongeren</p><p class=\"sra-case-list-item\">lagere inkomens</p><p class=\"sra-case-list-item\">vrouwen</p><p>Houd in de gehele opgave een betrouwbaarheid aan van 95%, tenzij anders aangegeven.</p><p>Een eerste indruk geeft de correlatietabel in afbeelding 1.</p><div class=\"sra-case-table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Correlations</th><th scope=\"col\"></th><th scope=\"col\"></th><th scope=\"col\"></th><th scope=\"col\"></th><th scope=\"col\"></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td>Korting</td><td>Leeftijd</td><td>Inkomen</td><td>Geslacht</td></tr><tr><td>Korting</td><td>Pearson Correlation</td><td>1</td><td>-,272**</td><td>-,725**</td><td>,617**</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Sig. (2-tailed)</td><td></td><td>,006</td><td>,000</td><td>,000</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td>N</td><td>100</td><td>100</td><td>100</td><td>100</td></tr><tr><td>Leeftijd</td><td>Pearson Correlation</td><td>-,272**</td><td>1</td><td>,541**</td><td>-,199*</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Sig. (2-tailed)</td><td>,006</td><td></td><td>,000</td><td>,048</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td>N</td><td>100</td><td>100</td><td>100</td><td>100</td></tr><tr><td>Inkomen</td><td>Pearson Correlation</td><td>-,725**</td><td>,541**</td><td>1</td><td>-,352**</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Sig. (2-tailed)</td><td>,000</td><td>,000</td><td></td><td>,000</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td>N</td><td>100</td><td>100</td><td>100</td><td>100</td></tr><tr><td>Geslacht</td><td>Pearson Correlation</td><td>,617**</td><td>-,199*</td><td>-,352**</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Sig. (2-tailed)</td><td>,000</td><td>,048</td><td>,000</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td>N</td><td>100</td><td>100</td><td>100</td><td>100</td></tr><tr><td>**. Correlation is significant at the 0.01 level (2-tailed).</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>*. Correlation is significant at the 0.05 level (2-tailed).</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"sra-case-caption\">Afbeelding 1</p></section>",
